MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The smart plug feels like a useful next purchase because it would let my existing Echo devices control a lamp, adding something I cannot already do with those devices alone.",
    "The Show 8 interests me because a larger screen could serve another room, while the Echo Flex offers a compact option for a hallway. Both suggest a distinct use beyond simply adding another speaker."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The older Fire TV devices, Show 5, and Echo Dot repeat needs covered by my recent 4K Max, second-generation Show 5, and fourth-generation Dot. Their similarity to what I own gives me little reason to choose them now.",
    "The earbuds do not connect to a current need I have expressed. My recent purchases concern home electronics and computer equipment, which does not mean I currently want personal listening gear."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repeated Alexa purchases seem to have been taken as interest in almost any Echo device, even when another speaker would add little to my setup.",
    "My Fire TV purchase seems to have been read as a reason to buy more streaming devices, overlooking that the recent purchase already filled that need."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The specific generations I recently chose matter: older versions are less appealing when I already have newer devices serving the same purpose.",
    "My Show 5 stand and past replacement batteries suggest that supporting and extending equipment I own can be more useful to me than buying another similar device. A new capability or a clear use in another room makes a stronger case."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my interest in an Alexa-connected home, but often treated recently fulfilled needs as reasons to recommend redundant devices."
}
